(5528581, 796248, 30982, '<td valign="top">Greetings from the Critique Club!<br/> <br/>Hi Nick and welcome to DPC!  This is a great idea for this challenge and I hope no kittens were harmed in the making of this photograph.  :-)  You obviously hit the "cute" button very well with this one.  The composition is pretty strong - it''s a great portrait of the dog and you did well to get a catchlight in the eye.  It could use a touch of levels or brightness to brighten it a bit, and a bit more sharpening - for the DPC crowd, tack sharp is usually rewarded.  Along that line, a slightly deeper DOF to get more of the kittens in crisper focus would add a bit as well.  Background is clean (ie uncluttered) and suits this well.<br/> <br/>Look forward to seeing more of your entries - if you have any questions, feel free to send me a PM!</td>', 'Greetings from the Critique Club! Hi Nick and welcome to DPC!  This is a great idea for this challenge and I hope no kittens were harmed in the making of this photograph.  :-)  You obviously hit the "cute" button very well with this one.  The composition is pretty strong - it''s a great portrait of the dog and you did well to get a catchlight in the eye.  It could use a touch of levels or brightness to brighten it a bit, and a bit more sharpening - for the DPC crowd, tack sharp is usually rewarded.  Along that line, a slightly deeper DOF to get more of the kittens in crisper focus would add a bit as well.  Background is clean (ie uncluttered) and suits this well. Look forward to seeing more of your entries - if you have any questions, feel free to send me a PM!', '2009-06-15 03:00:04.000000', NULL, 0),
(5528584, 793992, 30982, '<td valign="top">Greetings from the Critique Club!<br/> <br/>I''m going to guess that your low votes on this one were as much or more for subject matter than for the photograph itself.  It is kinda funny (I see you put it in the humorous gallery) but most probably don''t like to see drug use condoned, and one would question whether friends should let friends get stoned (as far as linking it to the challenge topic).  As for the photograph - yep, she definitely looks stoned!  I like the composition, especially with the OOF girl behind with the cards.  Makes me wonder what the game is, and whether or not she has a good hand (she looks like she does).  Perhaps a little snap-shot''ish, but I think snapshots are a valid form of photography.  You documented the moment well, and this has a silly "high" sort of feel to it.  It''s just not to the taste of your audience, I don''t think.</td>', 'Greetings from the Critique Club! I''m going to guess that your low votes on this one were as much or more for subject matter than for the photograph itself.  It is kinda funny (I see you put it in the humorous gallery) but most probably don''t like to see drug use condoned, and one would question whether friends should let friends get stoned (as far as linking it to the challenge topic).  As for the photograph - yep, she definitely looks stoned!  I like the composition, especially with the OOF girl behind with the cards.  Makes me wonder what the game is, and whether or not she has a good hand (she looks like she does).  Perhaps a little snap-shot''ish, but I think snapshots are a valid form of photography.  You documented the moment well, and this has a silly "high" sort of feel to it.  It''s just not to the taste of your audience, I don''t think.', '2009-06-15 03:10:19.000000', NULL, 0),
